# Build context for builder/Dockerfile. The context is the REPO ROOT (not builder/) because
# the Dockerfile COPYs config/portage/lock/builder.lock — see plan/15 layer 3.
#
# Everything below is either huge, machine-local, or both. out/ alone is tens of GB once a
# vendor archive exists, and Docker sends the whole context to the daemon before reading the
# first instruction.
out/
.git/
.claude/
